Subject: [PATCH 08477/11362] [outer-loop] ARC lever #5: wire the
 budget-exhaustion meter into the live path (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6180-WIRING)

Operator directive 2026-08-07. REQ-ARC-WMTE-6180 built the estimator
(arc_hud_bar_detector.budget_exhaustion_estimate) and its consumer
(arc_solver_kit.budget_aware_path_cost_weight), both genuinely tested, but
left them deliberately unwired -- the Phase Prototype discipline. This is
that wiring, still DEFAULT OFF pending an A/B.

Wired into StepwiseExplorer, not plan_in_model: the scored path's only
existing depth-cost term lives in _frontier (raw depth, hardcoded weight
1.0); plan_in_model has no depth-cost term at all (FIFO BFS / pure
best-first), so wiring there would mean adding an entire new cost
dimension rather than substituting an existing one.

Three pieces, all gated behind self.budget_aware_search_enabled (new
__init__ kwarg + _fd_gate ladder: explicit > CARNOT_ARC_BUDGET_AWARE_SEARCH
env > the kit's own BUDGET_AWARE_SEARCH_ENABLED, imported top-level, no
SUBMITTED_* mirror):
- PRODUCER: _ingest appends every raw frame to self._budget_frames
  unconditionally (one list.append, negligible); the ESTIMATE computation
  that consumes it runs only with the flag on and a HUD mask admitted,
  wrapped defensively (estimator exception -> None, never a crash).
- CONSUMER: _frontier computes depth_cost via budget_aware_path_cost_weight
  only when the flag is on, substituting it for the bare depth term across
  all four frontier key shapes; with the flag off depth_cost IS the literal
  depth expression, not an argument-shaped no-op -- the substitution itself
  is gated, not just consulted-value-happens-to-be-None.
- SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG gains budget_aware_search_enabled/_wired for
  readiness-gate visibility.

Scope narrowed from the fuller plumbing sketch, disclosed in the spec entry:
no explicit RESET marker in the frame buffer (_segment_frames's own
resegmentation rule handles it without one); evidence=None passed to the
estimator (lets it compute region_hud_evidence itself, a documented
fallback path) rather than threading through Stage-2's private admission
certificate. No E3AgentPolicy pass-through kwarg added -- the env rung
already reaches StepwiseExplorer directly and nothing yet needs
per-instance injection.

13 new tests covering the flag ladder, producer (buffer fill, gated
estimate computation, exception safety), and consumer (call-interception on
the mechanism itself, plus a stale-estimate-must-not-leak byte-identity
test). Broader regression sweep (139 tests across this file, the
estimator's own suite, the hazard-pruner precedent, goal-reinduction and
trajectory-transfer suites) all passing. scripts/arc_orphan_solver_lint.py
green (69 modules).

Artifact-freshness: 11 artifacts drifted on arc_competition_agent.py, same
uniform argument as lever #2's round -- flag-gated dead code plus one
strictly-additive unconditional list append -- + the usual second-order
metadata-only cascade. artifact-freshness-lint: OK.

